{
  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion → 0.4224 acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion actually adds value over a unimodal baseline. config_017 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is the cleanest single-axis comparison: it uses the same image encoder and profile setting as config_001, removing only the RNA modality and fusion step. If image-only achieves comparable accuracy, the RNA contribution (and all downstream RNA-encoder/fusion questions) is deprioritized; if it is substantially lower, multimodal fusion is confirmed as a productive direction and subsequent experiments can focus on optimizing RNA encoder, aggregation, and fusion. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the single most important architectural decision before spending further budget on finer-grained multimodal variants."
}

